# Datsun Cherry N10 three-door hatchback, 1978-1982.
#
# The third-generation Cherry, the first with a hatchback body, sold in Britain
# from 1978 as the Datsun Cherry. The three-door is modelled; the five-door has
# a different rear side glass and tailgate and is not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Cherry
#
# Dimensions 3.820 x 1.580 x 1.370 m, wheelbase 2.395 m, from the English
# Wikipedia third-generation (N10) dimension box. Handles take the modelled
# width to 1.601 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the N10 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: white, red, blue and silver. Weights white 3, red 3, blue 2,
# silver 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 140 km/h for the 1.2, the volume UK engine. Comfort 55/265, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 55, a step above the E10's 50/255 because the hatchback is roomier
# and rides better. Classes 0,1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: September 1978 intro, retires staggered 1994-1997 on a
# sixteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-n10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-n10.dae (44 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-cherry-n10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitation: image 1, the profile, is a low front three-quarter rather
# than a level side view, and no true profile of a three-door N10 exists on
# Commons. The proportions were reconciled against the published dimensions
# rather than measured off the photograph. At 128 px the round lamps, the
# horizontal grille and the three-door hatch outline read correctly.

